==Enemy==
[[Rain D.]]'s [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] variant with fewer knockbacks, can [[Knockback|knockback]] cat units and has a small boost in attack power and health. However, it both attacks and moves slower than its original counterpart.

==Strategy==
The only difference between fighting this enemy and Rain D. is its ability to knock back your cats and its classification as a Red enemy. [[Courier Cat|Courier Cat]] is the best unit to uninstall this enemy, with their quick attacks and spammability vaporizing Christmas D. in just a few hits. You can also use any [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]] variant ([[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]], [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Island Cat]], etc.) to kill this enemy quite quickly.

Spam meatshields (i.e. [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]], [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]]) and release [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Alternatively, you can also spam meatshields and stack [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cats]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]].

When trying to defeat Christmas D. quickly in order to earn the [[Timed Score Reward]]s, stack [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and other [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] varieties.

